 and spoke to a young version  of dead gamora after he snapped  a hint that the soul world could be  accessible perhaps of course there'd be  many fans who'd love for natasha to  return in a black widow sequel or even a  different movie and i think that  including the whistle response would  have given fans the impression that  marvel was committed to doing that  in some way which is my guess for why  they ultimately didn't do it  leave a thumbs up if you wish there'd  been a whistle response and let me know  whether you think natasha should come  back from the dead  the main events of the movie culminate  with team natasha taking out drakov  liberating his brainwashed widows and  crashing the airborne red room to the  ground  as secretary ross together with a large  military convoy heads towards the crash  site  nat sends her adoptive family and the  red room survivors away while she waits  to face  the music alone what exactly happens  next is left to our imagination as the  film cuts to black  before returning with an epilogue scene  set two weeks later that shows natasha  is still free  footage from the black widow trailers  however indicates that originally there  was an  alternate or extended version of this  ending where ross gets out to survey the  scene together with a swat team from the  beginning of the movie  you can see from the hungarian writing  on the truck behind ross that the red  room appeared to crash down somewhere in  hungary perhaps  even near budapest there's also deleted  footage in the trailers of armed  marksmen emerging from cars and scores  of military personnel taking up  positions among the wreckage of the red  room  with their sights presumably set on  natasha it seems like this would have  been an almost impossible situation for  natasha to escape from by herself  although given some of the crazy fun  action in the movie it's not  unfeasible to think that she would have  found a way out given she and hawkeye  survived a shootout with the hungarian  special forces  many years earlier it's also possible  that she somehow struck a deal with ross  or tricked him again in some way though  i don't think he'd be especially  amenable to a negotiation  there were some great moments with david  harbour's red guardian while he's locked  up in the russian prison and we find him  bragging about the supposed battles he  had with captain america  what year was this lady 384  captain america was still frozen in ice  then and the prison break scene when  natasha and elena come to rescue him  originally included more extensive red  guardian combat scenes  the marketing material shown fighting  other prisoners who got  out after a prison riot kicked off and  in some behind-the-scenes footage we can  also see alexi  fighting off a pack of prison guards  whereas in the final version red  guardian's only encounter with a guard  is while he's climbing at one of the  walls  i suspect the longer prison fight was  cut for time given the final movie was  already two and a quarter hours long  though personally i never felt the film  dragged some more red guardian moments  from the trailers that didn't make it  into the final movie include alexi  flexing and admiring his muscles in  molina's bathroom which is deleted from  the scene where he decides to put on his  old red guardian  suit we also don't get to see him  putting on his helmet as he does here in  the promos  and alexi's reaction after he leaves the  bathroom with his costume on  is noticeably different in the trailer  compared to the final movie  still fits  it still fits speaking to inverse  director kate shortland said that there  was a good deal of improvisation on set  especially during the dinner table  reunion and i found some more dialogue  by alexi for that scene in the trailers  that wasn't used in the final film  you got fat smelly water  in the final version of the movie this  is how that exchange goes instead  you got fat but still good i just got  out of the prison i  uh i have a lot of energy oh please  don't do that  also in the trailers but not in the  final film is footage of taskmaster  watching black widow fight and analyzing  her moves  it's called science taskmaster and that  line from elena did not make it into the  final film either  by the way the footage from that  cutscene is actually taken from  natasha's hallway fight in iron man 2.  in the final movie taskmaster analyzes  natasha's moves during the fight on the  bridge  rather than in advance and instead we  see the antagonist studying a hawkeye  fight scene which sets up the taskmaster  arrow attack on nat and elena in  budapest  there's also a small piece of dialogue  that drakov appears to say to taskmaster  in the trailers that wasn't in the final  film  this appears to imply that originally  part of taskmaster's mission was to  capture natasha or elena and take her to  the red room  rather than just retrieve the antidote  vials which was her main mission in the  finished film  the story of who was underneath the mask  and how she was part of natasha's red  ledger fitted well with the overall  theme of the movie about the abuse of  girls and women  however i think the movie's promotional  material led many fans to believe that  taskmaster was going to be a much  bigger villain for example the way one  trailer was cut even implied that  taskmaster was going to be the big bad  rather than drakov his call signs  taskmaster  he controls the red room i really  enjoyed the film however the marketing  may well have set the wrong expectations  for fans going into the movie when it  came to taskmaster's role  natasha and elena also had some deleted  and alternate versions of their scenes  in budapest  after their fight in the apartment this  quip from natasha was cut from the final  movie  it's good to see you too sis and then  there's a line from elena that appeared  in a lot of the promos for the film  natasha my sister after all this time  what brings you home i can see why this  was cut as it doesn't make a lot of  sense in the movie given it was elena  who sent natasha the vials of antidote  together with their childhood photo in  the first place so elena already knew  why natasha had come home  and there's also a deleted line from  elena's dialogue about what she imagined  natasha's life would have been like in  america  you're thinking about moving but you're  gonna wait until the interest rates go  down  we did get to briefly see some of the  red room widows training in unison  after team natasha arrived on the  floating platform  however as you might expect for any big  film like this  and as we can see from the trailers a  lot more footage was shot at the widow's  training choreography that didn't make  it into the final cut  and a cameo by tony stark was also  apparently on the cards according to a  september 2019 deadline report from the  saturn awards where it was stated that  quote  downey will be seen in the role of stark  one more time in the marvel prequel  black widow  clearly tony stark wasn't in the movie  although elena did mention him at one  point as one of natasha's avenger  scientist friends who she thought could  help analyze the mind control antidote  formula why don't you take it to one of  your super scientist friends  tony stark maybe given their final words  in civil war though  i doubt they'd have been on speaking  terms during the main events of black  widow  so i don't think it would have made a  lot of sense for him to appear in the  film  t'challa told ross what you did so  they're coming for you i'm not the one  that needs to watch their back  still possible scenarios where he might  have fit would have been via a flashback  or reusing footage from a previous movie  like when thor ragnarok used an age of  ultron cliff of natasha to calm the hulk  and bring banner back  alternately tony could have been a voice  over the phone similar to how hawkeye's  voice  was in the movie during the flashback to  the assassination attempt on drakov  we need confirmation takeoffs in the  building since recording this video kate  shortland has revealed in an interview  with gamesradar that initially there  were discussions about whether any of  the other avengers or existing marvel  characters should be involved in the  movie but in the end both she and kevin  feige agreed that quote  she doesn't need the boys we didn't want  it to feel like she needs the support we  want her to stand alone and she does  and if you want to see all the black  widow connections to the mcu which did  make it into the final movie things you  missed in the post-credits scenes and  the secret link between bucky and the  red room tap here to watch my black  widow  mcu changes video or follow the link in  the video description  so do you wish any of these deleted  scenes have been in the final movie and  do you think we'll ever see black widow  again  on screen comment with your thoughts  below and if you enjoyed this then do  like  and share the video i really appreciate  him you can tap left for my full black  widow breakdown  or tap right for another video you're  sure to like thanks for watching and see  you next time yippee guy movie lovers

